It is late.
"Goodnight, see you tomorrow," Nina says and goes home.
I am alone in my flat.
The two cups are still on the table.
But I am not tidying up now.
I turn off the kitchen light.
Now it is almost dark in the room.
Only the warm lamp by the window is on.
I sit down on the sofa.
I am tired after a long day.
But I am also very happy.
By the lamp stands the photo of my family.
My family in Mexico smiles at me.
They are far away, but I am not alone.
It is quiet and warm here.
"This is my home," I think and smile.
